Lumen — third-party software

Lumen is built on the open-source software listed here. Each entry gives the
version Lumen pins, its licence, and where the licence text is. Full texts are
in the LICENSES directory.

This file covers the components Lumen ships or drives directly. The complete,
machine-generated list of Rust crates and npm packages compiled into a release
is produced when the app is packaged and is shipped inside the app bundle as
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.


1. Playback engine and media libraries
======================================

These are compiled from source by scripts/build-deps.sh, at the versions and
commits pinned in that script, and shipped as dynamic libraries in
Lumen.app/Contents/Frameworks (and, for FFmpeg's tools, as separate programs).

mpv 0.42.0 (libmpv)                        https://mpv.io
    LGPL-2.1-or-later. Built with -Dgpl=false, which selects mpv's LGPL
    subset; no GPL-only part of mpv is compiled in.
    Text: LICENSES/mpv-LGPL-2.1.txt, LICENSES/mpv-Copyright.txt
