How the LGPL terms are met
--------------------------
libmpv and the FFmpeg libraries are separate dynamic libraries that Lumen
loads at run time; Lumen does not link them statically. FriBidi, libplacebo
and LAME are linked into those libraries, not into Lumen. You may replace any
of them with your own build: the exact sources, configuration and the one
patch are in scripts/build-deps.sh and scripts/patches, and running that
script reproduces the libraries Lumen ships.


2. Software Lumen runs but does not ship
========================================

yt-dlp                                     https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp
    Lumen uses yt-dlp to open and download online video. It is not included
    in the app: Lumen downloads the official release on first use, verifies
    its checksum, and runs it as a separate program.
    yt-dlp's source is released under the Unlicense. Its release binaries
    bundle other software and are, as a whole, licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later;
    see the yt-dlp project for the texts and sources.


Whisper "base" speech model, ggml-base-q5_1.bin
                                           https://github.com/openai/whisper
    Used to sync subtitles to a film's speech. It is not included in the
    app: Lumen downloads whisper.cpp's conversion of it from Hugging Face
    (https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp) the first time a subtitle
    is synced, checks its SHA-256, and runs it on the Mac. The model weights
    are released by OpenAI under the MIT licence.


